clean_summary:
Here is a great explanation of why the recent nature physics papers suggesting that neurons are simple are deeply misleading, both linguistically and statistically.

@Ansh_soni1234: "Simple input-output dependencies explain neuronal activity (@ChrisWLynn) has made the rounds on X with divided opinions. I show in this blog that while neurons are described simply, so can explicitly complex units: Describe and Arise are distinct claims."

Neurons may be describable by simple dependencies, but they do not arise solely from them, which challenges the idea that neurons are inherently simple.

